From 72aeecb663fd23ea5d08f24ea2b8988bcd4fb0dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mabn <github@mabn.pl>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:51:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lua: engine-side explosion and damage log a sandboxed widget
 can pull

A game's widget handler decides which callins reach a widget and with
which arguments. BAR's 2026.10.13 release gives user widgets a sandboxed
proxy of its handler, through which a widget can no longer install the
Explosion callin (projectile ids, ownerless explosions, LightningCannon
and DGun hits) nor read UnitDamaged's weapon, projectile and attacker.
It still hands user widgets a full copy of the Spring table.

So the engine records both itself, for any unsynced Lua handle that asks:

  Spring.SetEngineEventLog(explosions, damage)
  Spring.GetLoggedExplosions([fill]) -> values, count, dropped
  Spring.GetLoggedDamage([fill])     -> values, count, dropped

Two unsynced event clients copy numbers out of the events into vectors:
explosions at order -100, ahead of every Lua handle (Explosion dispatch
stops at the first client that claims one), damage at 1999, just before
LuaUI, so the post-hit health matches what a widget's own callin read.
Explosion returns false, nothing synced is read beyond what the event
hands over, and nothing is written, so the simulation and its graphics
are unchanged. Off by default (not registered); the getters return
nothing unless the caller has full read, so a playing client cannot see
enemy fire through them. LuaUI's destruction switches both off.
